    stickyCount     : INT := 0;
    prevPressureValid : BOOL := FALSE;
    prevPressure    : REAL := 0.0;
    prevFuelFlow    : REAL := 0.0;
    prevSteamFlow   : REAL := 0.0;
END_VAR

VAR_TEMP
    risingReset     : BOOL;
    causeMask       : WORD;
END_VAR
```

Now I need to detect a rising edge on the reset button and calculate the trip conditions. If the run request is active with either invalid pressure or pressure exceeding the threshold, the trip should latch. When the reset button transitions from low to high and the system conditions allow (runRequest off, pressure valid, and below the release threshold), the trip can be cleared.

The cause mask needs to capture why the trip occurred: transmitter failure, valve sticking, excess combustion, or unknown causes. The valve sticking detection requires the outlet command to be at least 50% while feedback stays at or below 10% for three consecutive scans while the system is running with valid pressure above threshold.

When the trip latches, I accumulate the current cause mask into the latched mask so it persists across cycles. Fuel permit becomes false whenever the trip is active, allowing it to be re-enabled only after the trip clears.

The diagnostic flag activates whenever any cause bit is set. Before completing the scan, I store the current reset button and run request states as previous values for edge detection on the next cycle.

